A||||11||Slick781||exhaust Qs, and Torque Qs||||1||
Z||000000||Slick781||04-15-2001||03:20 PM||||Ok... well on our 85 GT we just bought, we were lookin at the exhaust and noticed the cat had been removed, and there was a bad connection on the pipes, so i got to thinkin about new exhaust... <P>any advice on inexpensive good sounding exhaust?<P>also, while searchin on here, i found alot of people talking about certain exhaust systems and losing torque, how does all that work?  how do you lose torque from exhaust, and what are ways to gain torque overall (fairly inexpensive ways <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>thanky,<BR>david||||reg||1
Z||000001||Slick781||04-15-2001||06:49 PM||||anybody?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||04-15-2001||07:00 PM||||Hey David!<BR>Good question!<BR>If you use a header with short, large diameter primary tubes, you gain HP, but loose torque...<BR>And if you use long, skinny primary tubes you gain torque, but loose HP...<BR>When you add the colector, then you can balance out the gain and loss of torque or HP...<BR>Kinda scientific subject, you need to know the RPM range you want to play with and the base HP and torque you want...<BR>As to inexpensive, whats that???<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||04-15-2001||07:29 PM||||As often mentioned here, A cherry bomb muffler in place of the cat give you good performance and a fairly quiet sound without a lot of expense. Less than $20 at Pep Boys.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slick781||04-15-2001||07:43 PM||||ahh, thanx guys... when i said inexpensive, i just meant that i didnt want an exhaust system that's made for a race car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>basically what im lookin for is an exhaust system that will sound better (louder, meaner) than the stock exhaust, wont decrease performance, and will look good- actually i like the look of the stock tips..<P>don't want any rice boy "pissed off bumble bee" sound goin on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>ill do a forum search for these cherrybombs||||reg||1
Z||000005||Slick781||04-15-2001||07:46 PM||||by the way... we dont have any emissions tests here, to provide more info||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||04-16-2001||02:43 AM||||No emissions? <BR>Lucky dog.<P>I would have to say for a really good mellow sound at idle and a good snarl when you push the loud pedal to go to 2.5 inch exhaust (out here in California we usually put it just behind the exhaust) with your choice of straight pipe, cherry bomb or even a cat if you are so enviromentally concious with a flowmaster muffler. <P>Without the cat and driving...enthusiasticly...you might have a local representitive of the law enforcement chat with you about what you will do to increase revenue to the city...with the cherry bomb or cat you might get it just where you want it.<P>Loss of torque is essentially not enough backflow in the exhaust. The engine really doesn't have anything to "push" on if the rpms go up to fast. I found out the hard way that 2.5 inchpipes with JUST the cherry bomb flows too well and I could feel some loss of bottom end. Though freeway driving seems to breathe a little easier. <P>It is truly all about balance.<P>Oh BTW, since the jury still seems to be out about if certain headers do better than others the above suggestion is from my experience with an 88 GT with stock manifolds. Keith "Fiero Doc" Huff has a 3.4 with FOCOA headers 2.5" exhaust and flowmaster and sounds just as vicious. Though its hard to tell if he lost anything torque wise since he went bigger engine with 4.10 gears. My personal Fiero is a built up 2.8 with ported manifolds, cherry bomb (instead of cat) and 2.5" exhaust. Lost some torque on this so I might keep the bomb and add the flowmaster and tune the sound from that point. I have the pipes flanged to accept the cherry bomb, cat, or a straight pipe. I can tell you that this was the really expensive way to go! Experimentation can be that though!<P>Good luck to ya! Hope this helps.<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 04-16-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||Slick781||04-16-2001||07:59 PM||||hey, thanx man, its definatly VERY helpful<P>i have neither the age nor experience to know bout all this stuff, so im just learnin as i go  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>so lemme try to summarize what i should do for good sounding, fairly cheap exhaust with minimal torque loss.....<P>my cat is already off, so all i need to do is buy me a cherry bomb, flowmaster 2.5"?<P>and then im good to go?  anything else i need to know?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dave Gunsul||04-16-2001||10:30 PM||||The Fiero exhuast manifolds are very restrictive, I would suggest either getting<BR>headers or having the stock manifolds ported.<BR>If you decide to do either of these I would<BR>also suggest getting them jet hot coated.<BR>This helps speed exhuast flow but it also helps cool the Fiero engine compartment down.<P>A good exhuast will give you more torque and <BR>HP but a performance exhuast usually moves<BR>the torque curve higher in the RPM band.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000009||Slick781||04-16-2001||11:43 PM||||can ya give me some prices for both of those options? <P>i'm not exactly the wealthiest person on the block  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>i'm not exactly looking to try to burn every car on the street, yano... just that when my dad was checkin out the exhaust on the 85 we just bought, he noticed it was in pretty shoddy shape... so if we're going to need to replace it, im looking for something that will sound better than stock, and not break the bank...<P>thanx for the input  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>David||||reg||1
Z||000010||fyerstarter||04-17-2001||03:07 AM||||Headers for fieros are usually pretty expensive $400-$500.  It's rediculous. Thank god mine were already on when I bought my car :P<P>A few exhaust options:<P>Catwise:<P>-High Flow Cat (www.cwestco.com)  $80<BR>-Cherry Bomb  (Autozone, Pep Boyss, etc.) $20<P>Muffler Wise:<P>-80 Series Flowmaster of a Camaro  (www.summitracing.com) $80<BR>-40 Series Fiero Flowmaster $140 (www.cwestco.com)<BR>-West Coast Fiero High Flow Muffler S100 (www.cwestco.com)<P>Pipe Wise:<P>2.5 pipe from the Y pipe back $175  (www.cwestco.com)<P>Cat Back Systems:<P>Ocelot Performance Cat back exhaust system with tips $250  (www.fierostore.com)<P>Borla Cat back exhaust system with tips $550 (www.fieroparts.com)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Dave Gunsul||04-17-2001||08:09 PM||||Actually the price for headers is even worse<BR>than that. The Sprints are $550.00 and<BR>come with the coating already on them.<BR>F.O.C.O.A.'s headers (these are full length type) are $550.00 without coating and another<BR>$150.00 with the coating!<BR>So yes they are insainly priced but you gott-a pay to play. ;-)<BR>The bored out exhaust manifolds are much cheaper but offer less HP gain.<BR>Darrell Morse sells these for $150.00.<BR>You would have to send them in to Jet Hot to <BR>get the coating yourself. The coating will<BR>cost another hundred and some dollars but is<BR>worth the effort becuase of the heat in the Fiero's engine compartment.<BR>You can reach Darrell at:  morse86@aol.com<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
